<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdalonymus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdalonymus was king of Sidon, installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in 332 BCE. Ancient writers say he was a poor gardener of royal descent chosen in place of the deposed king Straton. The Alexander Sarcophagus, found at Sidon and now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>, is thought to have been made for him, and he ruled as a Macedonian client king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdalonymus.jpg" alt="Abdalonymus" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: derivative work: User:G.dallorto (talk) NAMABG-Colored_Alexander_Sarcophagus_1.JPG: Marsyas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Achaemenid_cavalry_on_Alexander_Sarcophagus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
